summary: Run upstream timetests in rhel kernel
description: |
    These are a collection of timekeeping tests assembled to try to provide
    some basic sanity testing of the timekeeping code.
    Areas covered include:
        Consistency check
        Raw skew check
        Nanosleep timers check
        Nanosleep latency check
        set_timer latency check
        Mqueue latency check
        Alarmtimer suspend check 
        Adjtimex basic validation tests
        Adjtimex freq adjustment tests
        Adjtimex tick adjustment tests
        Clocksource changing tests
        Leap second tests
        TAI setting tests
        Settimeofday edge cases
    Test Inputs:
        Original git site: https://github.com/johnstultz-work/timetests
        Downstream fork we use: https://github.com/linuxqiao/timetests
    Expected results:
        ++ grep FAILED /tmp/timetests.log
        + [[ -n '' ]]
        + rstrnt-report-result general/time/timetests_upstream PASS 0
    Results location:
        output.txt
contact: Qiao Zhao <qzhao@redhat.com>
id: 690bc9a4-890f-42fd-bf8b-49e5c32ca964
test: bash -x ./runtest.sh
framework: shell
require:
  - gcc
  - git
  - make
  - psmisc
duration: 240m
tier: 2
extra-summary: general/time/timetests_upstream
extra-task: general/time/timetests_upstream
